<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine gov't says wheat fertilization up.</title>
<headline>Argentine gov't says wheat fertilization up.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers used fertilizer on about 64.5 percent of their 1996/97 wheat crop, compared with just 50.6-percent fertilization the previous season, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday.</p>
<p>Farmers sowed 6.8 million hectares with wheat this season, compared with around five million hectares in 1995/96.</p>
<p>--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
